From: ashfordeOU <236818772+ashfordeOU@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 03:14:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] C7 GMAT: the kernel's state at the first node, and one Moon
 for GMAT

The gmat job's fourth run (Flight dynamics run 42549642686, at b099de4ea) reported every SPK state,
with two adapter faults. The first row was GMAT's default spacecraft state: GMAT loads an ephemeris
propagator's state only when it propagates, and the first report came first. The spacecraft now
takes one 1e-12 s step (SpkPropInit) before it. From the second row on, positions were tens of
metres off with velocities within about 1e-8 km/s: GMAT reads the spacecraft relative to the Earth
through the Moon of its planetary SPK and subtracts the Moon of its own DE405 reader. GMAT's solar
system now reads NAIF's de440s.bsp through SPICE (GMAT_PLANETARY_SPK), fetched by the workflow with
its SHA-256 checked and cached, so that both Moons come from one ephemeris.

The notebook writes gmat/spk_differences.csv (per node: epoch offset in seconds, GMAT minus written)
and states the first, interior and last nodes' differences in the report. RESULTS (C7) records the
run. The rule is unchanged.
